📁 include/ — Header Files Directory
This folder contains all shared interface declarations and configuration constants used across the ROBOT_COOK autonomous robotics project. These headers define critical behavior and pin mappings for motor control, servo actuation, movement sequencing, reflectance sensing, and general utility routines.

📄 File Overview
File	Purpose
config.h	Centralized configuration for hardware pin assignments, speed thresholds, rotation timing, and calibrated servo angles.
drive.h	Functions for motor control: directional driving, braking, turning, and rotation.
movement.h	High-level movement routines that coordinate tasks like moving between stations and executing the burger-building sequence.
sensors.h	Reflectance line sensor interface, including line detection logic and direction classification.
servos.h	Functions to operate servo motors for the robot’s claws, including grabbing, releasing, and angle management using a ServoControl struct.
utilities.h	Composite utilities that combine sensor and motor logic for path following, obstacle handling, and course completion logic.
README	(Template placeholder — superseded by this file.)

🔧 Usage
These headers are intended to be included in source files inside the /src/ directory. All modules are written in C++ and built using the PlatformIO environment targeting an ESP32.

Example:

#include "drive.h"
#include "config.h"

void setup() {
    initializeMotorPins();
    driveForwardStraight(driveSpeed);
}
📌 Notes
The project relies on a calibrated set of servo angles and drive speeds defined in config.h to ensure precise actuation.

movement.h and utilities.h provide high-level abstractions and should be used to script complex behaviors rather than duplicating low-level commands.

All directional enums (e.g., FORWARD, LEFT) are declared in sensors.h.
